<!--
  The Naomi mark, traced from assets/logo_sheet.png.

  The sheet is a flattened 6 MB raster with no vector source, so the artwork was
  recovered by thresholding its 512px rendering and tracing the contours, then
  simplified until the polygon was indistinguishable from the original at every
  size a launcher uses. 120 points: finer made no visible difference, coarser
  faceted the ring.

  Colours are the app's, not the sheet's. The sheet specifies #5F8BB0 and a warm
  #343432, neither of which appears anywhere else in Naomi. Using them would have
  created a third answer to "what colour is Naomi" — exactly the ambiguity
  values/colors.xml records having just removed. Ink is onBackground; the dot is
  the slate primary the orb already uses.

  The mark is 56 units across in a 108 viewport. That is comfortably inside the
  72dp safe zone every launcher mask keeps, and was chosen against 62 and 50
  rendered inside a circular mask — 62 crowded the edge, 50 floated.
-->
